From: dm1q mainline port <dm1q-mainline@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: max77705: accept PMIC revision Pass2

The Samsung Galaxy S23 (SM-S911B, dm1q) carries a MAX77705 whose revision
register reads 0x2 (Pass2). The driver only accepted Pass3 and failed the probe
with "Rev.0x2 is not tested", so neither the MFD nor the charger and fuel gauge
that depend on it (deferred probe: supplier not ready) came up and the phone had
no battery.

Samsung's downstream driver supports this chip (its table lists MD15 PASS2 next
to MD05 PASS3/PASS4) and its charger and fuel gauge drivers contain no
revision-specific code; the revision only selects the USB-C controller firmware
update path, which mainline does not have. Accept Pass2 in addition to Pass3.

---
diff --git a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
--- a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	pmic_rev = pmic_rev_value & MAX77705_REVISION_MASK;
-	if (pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS3)
+	if (pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS2 && pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS3)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "Rev.0x%x is not tested\n", pmic_rev);
 
 	/* Active Discharge Enable */
-- 
